From: local emulation
Subject: stacktrace: replace xpaclri with backwards-compatible hint #7

Linaro 7.5-2019.12 ships binutils 2.32 whose aarch64 assembler does not
yet recognize the ARMv8.3-A `xpaclri` mnemonic; the same instruction is
encoded as the NOP `hint #7` on ARMv8.0+, which both the older binutils
and a PAuth-enabled CPU handle correctly.

--- a/absl/debugging/internal/stacktrace_aarch64-inl.inc
+++ b/absl/debugging/internal/stacktrace_aarch64-inl.inc
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ inline void* ClearPacBits(void* ptr) {
   // compatibility with ARM platforms that do not support pointer
   // authentication, we use the hint space instruction XPACLRI instead. Hint
   // space instructions behave as NOPs on unsupported platforms.
-  asm("xpaclri" : "+r"(x30));
+  asm("hint #7" : "+r"(x30));
   return x30;
 }

